config SPRD_CAMERA_SENSOR_P21H170_RAILS
	bool "Enable the p21h170 camera sensor workarounds"
	default n
	help
	  Enable this on p21h170 only. Leave it disabled on p22h190 so its
	  behaviour is completely unchanged.

	  Two gaps were found in how the factory camera HAL and this sensor
	  driver split the power-up sequence. Both are gaps on the driver side,
	  verified against the HAL's own ioctl traffic:

	  1. The HAL never enables the sensor master clock. It only ever issues
	     SENSOR_IO_SET_MCLK with 0, and it never sends SENSOR_IO_POWER_CFG
	     (the command that would have carried the full sequence). The
	     factory kernel ran its own power-on sequence from that command;
	     this driver generation has it commented out. Without a running
	     MCLK the sensor cannot answer on i2c at all, so the driver enables
	     24MHz (select_sensor_mclk() takes MHz, and 24 is the value
	     libsensor_s5k4h7_tsp.so asks for) once the rails are up.

	  2. The camera i2c pins are only ever programmed by
	     sprd_pull_i2c_gpio(), which hangs off SENSOR_IO_SET_ID. The device
	     tree declares no pinctrl for the i2c nodes, so the bus depends on
	     that call reaching the driver. The driver now also programs the
	     pins itself when the rails come up.

	  Note: this does NOT make the camera work on the p21h170 unit that was
	  debugged - the sensor still does not acknowledge on i2c. The changes
	  are kept because they are verified, reasoned gaps, and the full
	  investigation is written up in device/eebbk/p21h170/CAMERA-NOTES.md.

endmenu
